  "output": "# Test Coverage Analysis — Havo\n\n**Bottom line: 0% coverage.** `package.json` already wires up `\"test\": \"node --test tests/\"`, but no `tests/` directory exists anywhere in the repo — every function below has literally never been executed by an automated test. This is a Next.js 16 / React 19 app (`\"type\": \"module\"`), so tests should be ESM, using Node's built-in `node:test` + `node:assert/strict` (no devDependency for Jest/Vitest is installed).\n\n## Test infrastructure gap (fix first)\n\n| Gap | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| No `tests/` directory | `npm test` currently fails/no-ops — nothing to run. |\n| No DOM test environment | `hooks/*`, `lib/scroll.js`, `features/*Store.js` touch `window`, `document`, `localStorage`, `matchMedia`, `IntersectionObserver`. `node:test` alone can't exercise these — needs either (a) hand-rolled fakes for the few globals used, or (b) `jsdom`/`@testing-library/react` added as a devDependency for hook/component tests. Nothing like that is installed. |\n| No component-rendering tooling | Zero devDependency for React Testing Library — all `.js` files under `components/`, `features/*/*.js` that return JSX are untestable as-is beyond extracting their pure helpers. |\n\nRecommended minimal setup to unblock everything below:\n```\ntests/\n  lib/format.test.js\n  lib/storage.test.js\n  lib/airQuality/waqi.test.js\n  features/impact/impact.test.js\n  features/progress/progress.test.js\n  features/progress/store.test.js\n  features/actions/finder.test.js\n  features/initiatives/proposal.test.js\n  features/problem/inversionSim.test.js\n  app/api/air-quality/route.test.js\n```\n\n---\n\n## Priority ranking\n\n| Priority | Module | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| P0 | `features/progress/progress.js` | Core reducer: points, streaks, badges, persistence sanitization. Most logic, most user-facing (gamification), silent corruption risk. |\n| P0 | `lib/airQuality/waqi.js` | Parses untrusted third-party JSON; a shape change in the external API silently breaks the dashboard or (worse) shows wrong AQI. |\n| P1 | `app/api/air-quality/route.js` | Only server route; no test hits any of its branches (missing token, bad city, upstream failure, timeout). |\n| P1 | `features/impact/impact.js` | User-facing CO₂ math; a sign/unit error would silently show wrong numbers. |\n| P1 | `features/actions/finder.js` | Recommendation ranking/filtering — easy to break silently when `data/actions.js` content changes. |\n| P2 | `features/initiatives/proposal.js` | Input validation with regexes (contact-info scrubbing) — regex edge cases are exactly where this breaks. |\n| P2 | `features/progress/store.js` | Integration: persistence, cross-tab sync, SSR/hydration snapshot. |\n| P3 | `features/problem/inversionSim.js` | Deterministic (seeded RNG) — eminently testable, currently untested. |\n| P3 | `lib/format.js`, `lib/storage.js` | Small, pure, cheap to cover; `format.js` has real Russian-pluralization edge cases. |\n| P4 | `features/planner/planItems.js`, `data/cities.js`, `features/*TabStore.js` | Trivial but zero-cost to add. |\n\n---\n\n## 1. `lib/format.js`\n\n**Untested functions:** `plural`, `pluralize`, `formatNumber`, `formatDate`, `formatDateTime`, `dayKey`, `timeAgo`, `daysUntil`, `deadlineLabel`.\n\n**Edge cases not covered:**\n- `plural`: n=0, n=11 (should be forms[2], not forms[1] — the `abs > 10 && abs < 20` teen exception), n=21 (forms[0]), negative n.\n- `formatNumber`: `NaN`, `Infinity`, `-Infinity` → `'—'`.\n- `formatDate`/`formatDateTime`: invalid date string → `'—'`.\n- `dayKey`: must use **local** time, not UTC (a date near midnight could differ by a day if implemented with UTC methods — worth locking down with a fixed timezone-sensitive date).\n- `timeAgo`: boundary at exactly 1 minute, 60 minutes, 24 hours; invalid input.\n- `daysUntil`: `null`/empty deadline, malformed string (not `YYYY-MM-DD`), exact today, past date.\n- `deadlineLabel`: tone mapping for danger/warn/neutral at the 0/1/negative boundaries.\n\n**Test skeleton:**\n```js\nimport { test, describe } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { plural, pluralize, formatNumber, formatDate, formatDateTime, dayKey, timeAgo, daysUntil, deadlineLabel } from '../../lib/format.js';\n\ndescribe('plural', () => {\n  test('n=1 -> singular form', () => assert.equal(plural(1, ['a','b','c']), 'a'));\n  test('n=2..4 -> form[1]', () => assert.equal(plural(2, ['a','b','c']), 'b'));\n  test('n=5..20 -> form[2] (teen exception)', () => assert.equal(plural(11, ['a','b','c']), 'c'));\n  test('n=21 -> form[0] again', () => assert.equal(plural(21, ['a','b','c']), 'a'));\n  test('n=0 -> form[2]', () => assert.equal(plural(0, ['a','b','c']), 'c'));\n  test('negative n uses abs value', () => assert.equal(plural(-1, ['a','b','c']), 'a'));\n});\n\ndescribe('formatNumber', () => {\n  test('NaN/Infinity -> em dash', () => {\n    assert.equal(formatNumber(NaN), '—');\n    assert.equal(formatNumber(Infinity), '—');\n  });\n  test('respects maximumFractionDigits', () => assert.equal(formatNumber(1.236, 2), '1,24'));\n});\n\ndescribe('formatDate/formatDateTime', () => {\n  test('invalid date -> em dash', () => {\n    assert.equal(formatDate('not-a-date'), '—');\n    assert.equal(formatDateTime('not-a-date'), '—');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('dayKey', () => {\n  test('uses local calendar day, zero-padded', () => {\n    assert.equal(dayKey(new Date(2026, 0, 5)), '2026-01-05');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('timeAgo', () => {\n  test('< 1 min -> \"только что\"', () => assert.equal(timeAgo(Date.now() - 1000), 'только что'));\n  test('boundary at 60 min switches to hours', () => {\n    const now = Date.now();\n    assert.match(timeAgo(now - 60 * 60000, now), /час/);\n  });\n  test('invalid input -> em dash', () => assert.equal(timeAgo('garbage'), '—'));\n});\n\ndescribe('daysUntil / deadlineLabel', () => {\n  test('null deadline -> null', () => assert.equal(daysUntil(null), null));\n  test('overdue -> negative days, danger tone', () => {\n    const now = new Date(2026, 9, 14);\n    assert.equal(daysUntil('2026-10-10', now), -4);\n    assert.equal(deadlineLabel('2026-10-10', now).tone, 'danger');\n  });\n  test('today -> tone warn, text \"сегодня\"', () => {\n    const now = new Date(2026, 9, 14);\n    assert.equal(deadlineLabel('2026-10-14', now).text, 'сегодня');\n  });\n  test('malformed deadline string -> null', () => assert.equal(daysUntil('not-a-date'), null));\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. `lib/storage.js`\n\n**Untested functions:** `readJSON`, `writeJSON`, `createId`.\n\n**Edge cases / error handling not covered:**\n- `typeof window === 'undefined'` (SSR) path — both read and write must return `null`/`false` without throwing.\n- Corrupted JSON in localStorage (`JSON.parse` throws) → must swallow and return `null`, not crash the page (this is the whole stated purpose of the module, per its own header comment, and it's untested).\n- `localStorage.setItem` throwing (quota exceeded / private browsing Safari) → `writeJSON` must return `false`, not throw.\n- `createId`: prefix defaulting, uniqueness-ish shape check, fallback path when `crypto.randomUUID` is unavailable.\n\n**Test skeleton:**\n```js\nimport { test, describe, mock } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { readJSON, writeJSON, createId } from '../lib/storage.js';\n\ndescribe('readJSON', () => {\n  test('returns null when window is undefined (SSR)', () => {\n    assert.equal(readJSON('k'), null); // no window in node:test by default\n  });\n\n  test('returns null on corrupted JSON without throwing', (t) => {\n    global.window = { localStorage: { getItem: () => '{not json' } };\n    t.after(() => { delete global.window; });\n    assert.doesNotThrow(() => assert.equal(readJSON('k'), null));\n  });\n\n  test('parses valid JSON', (t) => {\n    global.window = { localStorage: { getItem: () => '{\"a\":1}' } };\n    t.after(() => { delete global.window; });\n    assert.deepEqual(readJSON('k'), { a: 1 });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('writeJSON', () => {\n  test('returns false when window is undefined', () => assert.equal(writeJSON('k', {}), false));\n\n  test('returns false (not throw) when setItem throws (quota/private mode)', (t) => {\n    global.window = { localStorage: { setItem: () => { throw new Error('QuotaExceededError'); } } };\n    t.after(() => { delete global.window; });\n    assert.equal(writeJSON('k', { a: 1 }), false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('createId', () => {\n  test('uses default prefix \"id\"', () => assert.match(createId(), /^id-/));\n  test('custom prefix is applied', () => assert.match(createId('plan'), /^plan-/));\n  test('falls back to Math.random when crypto.randomUUID is unavailable', (t) => {\n    const realCrypto = global.crypto;\n    global.crypto = undefined;\n    t.after(() => { global.crypto = realCrypto; });\n    assert.match(createId('x'), /^x-[0-9a-z]+-[0-9a-z]+$/);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. `lib/airQuality/waqi.js` — highest-risk untested module\n\n**Untested functions:** `haversineKm`, `safeUrl` (not exported — test indirectly), `normalizeWaqi`, `epaCategory`.\n\n**Edge cases not covered (this is parsing untrusted external JSON — every branch matters):**\n- `json.status !== 'ok'` → error with `reason` taken from `data` string, vs `'invalid-response'` fallback when `data` isn't a string.\n- `data` is `null`/not an object.\n- `geo` array missing, has non-numeric entries, or only one element.\n- Station farther than `maxStationDistanceKm` → `'no-station'`, with `distanceKm` **rounded to integer** (note: this differs from the `'ok'` path which rounds to 1 decimal — easy regression target).\n- Missing/invalid `time.iso` → `'missing-timestamp'`.\n- `aqi` null AND all `iaqi` indices missing → `'no-data'`.\n- Indices partially present (only `pm25`) — others must be omitted from the `indices` object, not set to `null`.\n- `dominentpol` value not in `POLLUTANT_KEYS` → `dominant: null`.\n- `stale` boolean computed correctly at the `staleAfterHours` boundary (just under / just over).\n- `attributions`: non-array, entries missing `name`/`url`, invalid URL scheme (`javascript:`), truncation to 6 entries, name truncated to 120 chars.\n- `safeUrl`: `ftp://` or `javascript:` scheme rejected, malformed URL string rejected, non-string input rejected — this guards against XSS via attacker-controlled `url`/`attributions[].url` rendered as `<a href>` in `AirDashboard.js`; worth a dedicated security-flavored test.\n- `station.name` truncated to 160 chars; missing name falls back to `'Станция без названия'`.\n- `haversineKm`: same point → 0; antipodal-ish sanity check against a known city pair.\n- `epaCategory`: boundary values exactly at 50/100/150/200/300; non-numeric/NaN input → `null`.\n\n**Test skeleton:**\n```js\nimport { test, describe } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { normalizeWaqi, epaCategory, haversineKm } from '../../lib/airQuality/waqi.js';\n\nconst city = { id: 'tashkent', lat: 41.2995, lon: 69.2401 };\nconst opts = { maxStationDistanceKm: 40, staleAfterHours: 3, now: Date.parse('2026-10-14T12:00:00Z') };\n\nfunction baseJson(overrides = {}) {\n  return {\n    status: 'ok',\n    data: {\n      aqi: 85,\n      dominentpol: 'pm25',\n      city: { name: 'Tashkent', geo: [41.3, 69.24], url: 'https://aqicn.org/city/tashkent' },\n      time: { iso: '2026-10-14T11:00:00+00:00' },\n      iaqi: { pm25: { v: 85 }, pm10: { v: 40 } },\n      attributions: [{ name: 'UzHydromet', url: 'https://monitoring.meteo.uz' }],\n      ...overrides,\n    },\n  };\n}\n\ndescribe('normalizeWaqi error paths', () => {\n  test('status !== ok -> error with upstream reason string', () => {\n    const r = normalizeWaqi({ status: 'error', data: 'Invalid key' }, city, opts);\n    assert.deepEqual(r, { status: 'error', reason: 'Invalid key' });\n  });\n  test('status !== ok and data not a string -> invalid-response', () => {\n    const r = normalizeWaqi({ status: 'error', data: null }, city, opts);\n    assert.equal(r.reason, 'invalid-response');\n  });\n  test('null json -> error', () => assert.equal(normalizeWaqi(null, city, opts).status, 'error'));\n  test('missing geo -> missing-station-location', () => {\n    const json = baseJson(); delete json.data.city.geo;\n    assert.equal(normalizeWaqi(json, city, opts).reason, 'missing-station-location');\n  });\n  test('station farther than maxStationDistanceKm -> no-station, integer-rounded distance', () => {\n    const json = baseJson({ city: { name: 'Far', geo: [55, 60] } });\n    const r = normalizeWaqi(json, city, opts);\n    assert.equal(r.status, 'no-station');\n    assert.equal(Number.isInteger(r.station.distanceKm), true);\n  });\n  test('invalid time.iso -> missing-timestamp', () => {\n    const json = baseJson({ time: { iso: 'not-a-date' } });\n    assert.equal(normalizeWaqi(json, city, opts).reason, 'missing-timestamp');\n  });\n  test('no aqi and no indices -> no-data', () => {\n    const json = baseJson({ aqi: null, iaqi: {} });\n    assert.equal(normalizeWaqi(json, city, opts).status, 'no-data');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('normalizeWaqi happy path', () => {\n  test('partial indices omit missing pollutants (not null)', () => {\n    const json = baseJson({ iaqi: { pm25: { v: 60 } } });\n    const r = normalizeWaqi(json, city, opts);\n    assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(r.indices), ['pm25']);\n  });\n  test('dominentpol outside POLLUTANT_KEYS -> dominant null', () => {\n    const json = baseJson({ dominentpol: 'co' });\n    assert.equal(normalizeWaqi(json, city, opts).dominant, null);\n  });\n  test('stale flag true just past staleAfterHours boundary', () => {\n    const json = baseJson({ time: { iso: '2026-10-14T08:59:59+00:00' } }); // > 3h before `now`\n    assert.equal(normalizeWaqi(json, city, opts).stale, true);\n  });\n  test('rejects javascript: URLs in attributions (XSS guard)', () => {\n    const json = baseJson({ attributions: [{ name: 'evil', url: 'javascript:alert(1)' }] });\n    assert.deepEqual(normalizeWaqi(json, city, opts).attributions, []);\n  });\n  test('attributions capped at 6 entries', () => {\n    const many = Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, i) => ({ name: `s${i}`, url: 'https://x.com' }));\n    const json = baseJson({ attributions: many });\n    assert.equal(normalizeWaqi(json, city, opts).attributions.length, 6);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('epaCategory', () => {\n  for (const [v, id] of [[50,'good'],[51,'moderate'],[150,'usg'],[151,'unhealthy'],[301,'hazardous']]) {\n    test(`aqi=${v} -> ${id}`, () => assert.equal(epaCategory(v).id, id));\n  }\n  test('NaN/non-number -> null', () => assert.equal(epaCategory(NaN), null));\n});\n\ndescribe('haversineKm', () => {\n  test('same point -> ~0', () => assert.ok(haversineKm(41, 69, 41, 69) < 1e-9));\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. `app/api/air-quality/route.js` — integration gap (zero HTTP-level tests)\n\n**Untested behavior / error handling:**\n- Unknown `city` query param → 400 `{status:'error', reason:'unknown-city'}`.\n- Missing `city` param entirely.\n- No API token configured → 200 `{status:'unconfigured'}` (never leaks absence-of-token as an error).\n- Upstream non-OK HTTP status → 502 with `reason: upstream-${status}`.\n- Upstream fetch throws `TimeoutError` (via `AbortSignal.timeout`) → `reason: 'timeout'`.\n- Upstream fetch throws a generic network error → `reason: 'network'`.\n- Upstream returns invalid JSON (`res.json()` rejects) — currently **unhandled**: this would throw inside the try block before reaching the catch's `reason` logic... actually it's inside the try, so it *is* caught, but mapped to `reason: 'network'` even though it's a parse error — worth a test to document/confirm current (possibly misleading) behavior.\n- Response always sets `Cache-Control: no-store` — verify on every branch.\n- The token itself must never leak into the response body (regression guard).\n\n**Test skeleton** (mock global `fetch`; route reads `process.env` directly, so set/delete env var per test):\n```js\nimport { test, describe, mock } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { GET } from '../../../app/api/air-quality/route.js';\n\nfunction req(qs) {\n  return new Request(`http://localhost/api/air-quality${qs}`);\n}\n\ndescribe('GET /api/air-quality', () => {\n  test('unknown city -> 400', async () => {\n    const res = await GET(req('?city=mars'));\n    assert.equal(res.status, 400);\n    assert.deepEqual(await res.json(), { status: 'error', reason: 'unknown-city' });\n  });\n\n  test('missing city param -> 400', async () => {\n    const res = await GET(req(''));\n    assert.equal(res.status, 400);\n  });\n\n  test('no token configured -> unconfigured, 200, never calls fetch', async (t) => {\n    delete process.env.WAQI_API_TOKEN;\n    const fetchMock = t.mock.method(global, 'fetch');\n    const res = await GET(req('?city=tashkent'));\n    assert.equal(res.status, 200);\n    assert.deepEqual(await res.json(), { status: 'unconfigured' });\n    assert.equal(fetchMock.mock.callCount(), 0);\n  });\n\n  test('upstream non-OK status -> 502 with status code in reason', async (t) => {\n    process.env.WAQI_API_TOKEN = 'test-token';\n    t.after(() => delete process.env.WAQI_API_TOKEN);\n    t.mock.method(global, 'fetch', async () => new Response(null, { status: 503 }));\n    const res = await GET(req('?city=tashkent'));\n    assert.equal(res.status, 502);\n    assert.equal((await res.json()).reason, 'upstream-503');\n  });\n\n  test('upstream timeout -> reason timeout', async (t) => {\n    process.env.WAQI_API_TOKEN = 'test-token';\n    t.after(() => delete process.env.WAQI_API_TOKEN);\n    t.mock.method(global, 'fetch', async () => {\n      const e = new Error('timeout'); e.name = 'TimeoutError'; throw e;\n    });\n    const res = await GET(req('?city=tashkent'));\n    assert.equal((await res.json()).reason, 'timeout');\n  });\n\n  test('generic network failure -> reason network', async (t) => {\n    process.env.WAQI_API_TOKEN = 'test-token';\n    t.after(() => delete process.env.WAQI_API_TOKEN);\n    t.mock.method(global, 'fetch', async () => { throw new Error('ECONNRESET'); });\n    const res = await GET(req('?city=tashkent'));\n    assert.equal((await res.json()).reason, 'network');\n  });\n\n  test('token never appears in response body', async (t) => {\n    process.env.WAQI_API_TOKEN = 'super-secret-token';\n    t.after(() => delete process.env.WAQI_API_TOKEN);\n    t.mock.method(global, 'fetch', async () => new Response(null, { status: 503 }));\n    const res = await GET(req('?city=tashkent'));\n    const text = JSON.stringify(await res.json());\n    assert.doesNotMatch(text, /super-secret-token/);\n  });\n\n  test('every response sets Cache-Control: no-store', async (t) => {\n    const res = await GET(req('?city=mars')); // 400 path\n    assert.equal(res.headers.get('cache-control'), 'no-store');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. `features/impact/impact.js`\n\n**Untested functions:** `getAlternative`, `savingPerKm`, `calculateImpact`, `roundKg`.\n\n**Edge cases not covered:**\n- `clamp` behavior via `calculateImpact`: inputs below `min`, above `max`, `NaN`/non-finite → falls back to `min` (verify, since this silently changes the number shown to users).\n- Unknown `alternative` id → falls back to `ALTERNATIVES[0]` (`walk`), not an error.\n- `carpool` branch uses `shareOfCar` path (different formula arm) — distinct from `walk`/`bike`/`bus` which use `altLow`/`altHigh`; both arms need coverage, and `isRange` must be `false` for carpool (point estimate) and `walk`/`bike` (0,0 range), but `true` for `bus`.\n- `weeks <= 12` vs `weeks > 12` series-generation branches (different week-numbering logic, the latter uses evenly spaced checkpoints and rounds `week`).\n- `activeHours`: `null` for `carpool` (no `speedKmh`), numeric for others.\n- `roundKg`: `kg <= 0` → 0; `kg < 1` → 1-decimal rounding; large `kg` (e.g. 12345) → verify \"2 significant figures\" rounding (`Math.floor(Math.log10(kg))-1` magnitude) at power-of-10 boundaries (kg=10, kg=100 exactly) and for `NaN`/`Infinity`.\n\n**Test skeleton:**\n```js\nimport { test, describe } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { calculateImpact, savingPerKm, getAlternative, roundKg, CALC_LIMITS } from '../../features/impact/impact.js';\n\ndescribe('getAlternative', () => {\n  test('unknown id falls back to first alternative (walk)', () => {\n    assert.equal(getAlternative('spaceship').id, 'walk');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('savingPerKm', () => {\n  test('carpool uses shareOfCar formula (point estimate, not a range)', () => {\n    const [low, high] = savingPerKm('carpool', 200);\n    assert.equal(low, high);\n    assert.equal(low, 100);\n  });\n  test('bus returns a [low,high] range from 0 to car-bus delta', () => {\n    const [low, high] = savingPerKm('bus', 249);\n    assert.equal(low, 249 - 104);\n    assert.equal(high, 249);\n  });\n  test('never returns negative values even if altHigh > carFactor', () => {\n    const [low] = savingPerKm('bus', 50); // carFactor < bus factor\n    assert.ok(low >= 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('calculateImpact clamping', () => {\n  test('out-of-range tripsPerWeek is clamped to limits', () => {\n    const r = calculateImpact({ tripsPerWeek: 999, alternative: 'walk' });\n    assert.equal(r.inputs.tripsPerWeek, CALC_LIMITS.trips.max);\n  });\n  test('non-finite carFactor falls back to min', () => {\n    const r = calculateImpact({ carFactor: NaN, alternative: 'walk' });\n    assert.equal(r.inputs.carFactor, CALC_LIMITS.carFactor.min);\n  });\n  test('unknown alternative id does not throw, defaults to walk', () => {\n    assert.doesNotThrow(() => calculateImpact({ alternative: 'teleport' }));\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('calculateImpact series generation', () => {\n  test('weeks <= 12 -> one column per week', () => {\n    const r = calculateImpact({ weeks: 5, alternative: 'walk' });\n    assert.deepEqual(r.series.map((s) => s.week), [1,2,3,4,5]);\n  });\n  test('weeks > 12 -> 12 evenly spaced checkpoints', () => {\n    const r = calculateImpact({ weeks: 52, alternative: 'walk' });\n    assert.equal(r.series.length, 12);\n    assert.equal(r.series[11].week, 52);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('calculateImpact isRange / activeHours', () => {\n  test('walk/bike: isRange false (0 spread)', () => {\n    assert.equal(calculateImpact({ alternative: 'walk' }).isRange, false);\n  });\n  test('bus: isRange true', () => {\n    assert.equal(calculateImpact({ alternative: 'bus' }).isRange, true);\n  });\n  test('carpool: activeHours is null (no speedKmh)', () => {\n    assert.equal(calculateImpact({ alternative: 'carpool' }).activeHours, null);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('roundKg', () => {\n  test('zero/negative -> 0', () => { assert.equal(roundKg(0), 0); assert.equal(roundKg(-5), 0); });\n  test('< 1 -> one decimal', () => assert.equal(roundKg(0.456), 0.5));\n  test('exact power of 10 boundary', () => assert.equal(roundKg(100), 100));\n  test('NaN/Infinity -> 0', () => { assert.equal(roundKg(NaN), 0); assert.equal(roundKg(Infinity), 0); });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. `features/progress/progress.js` — highest-value target\n\n**Untested functions:** `sanitizeState` (+ its private sanitizers), `reducer` (11 action types), `computePoints`, `computeStreak`, `weekStart`, `completionsInWeek`, `bestWeekCount` (not exported — test via `computeBadges`'s `'weekly'` badge), `computeBadges` (8 badges), `computeMilestones`, `planStats`, `isInPlan`.\n\n**Edge cases not covered:**\n- `sanitizeState(null | undefined | \"garbage\" | [] | {malicious: '<script>'})` — must never throw, always returns a valid shape. This is the data coming straight out of `localStorage`, i.e. attacker/corruption-controlled.\n- `sanitizePlanItem`: missing `id`/`refId` → filtered out (`null`→dropped by `.filter(Boolean)`); `difficulty` out of `[1,3]` clamps; `deadline` not matching `YYYY-MM-DD` regex → `null`; oversized strings truncated to documented max lengths.\n- `sanitizeHistoryEntry`: missing `completedAt` or invalid ISO date → dropped.\n- `checklists` sanitization: non-array values dropped; indices outside `[0,50)` filtered; keys truncated to 80 chars.\n- `reducer('ADD_PLAN_ITEM')` when the same `(kind, refId)` already exists → **no-op**, returns the *same* state reference (important: `dispatch` in `store.js` checks `next === state` to skip persisting/emitting — a regression here breaks the \"already in plan\" dedup silently).\n- `reducer('TOGGLE_COMPLETE')` toggling an item that doesn't exist → no-op; toggling off removes the matching `history` entry by `planItemId` (verify no other history entries are touched).\n- `reducer('REMOVE_PLAN_ITEM')` explicitly preserves `history` (per the inline comment) — needs a regression test since it's an easy \"cleanup\" to accidentally \"fix\".\n- `reducer('RECORD_QUIZ')`: `bestScore` only updates on improvement, not on a worse re-attempt; first-ever attempt (`prevBest === null`) sets `bestScore` directly even if `score` is 0.\n- `reducer('RESET_PROGRESS')`: preserves `proposals` explicitly, resets everything else — this is a notable \"gotcha\" worth locking down.\n- `reducer` with an unknown action `type` → returns the same `state` unchanged.\n- `computePoints`: `bestScore` null → contributes 0 (not `NaN`); proposals capped at `MAX_COUNTED_PROPOSALS` (3) even if more exist.\n- `computeStreak`: empty history → `{current:0, best:0}`; single-day history; a gap in the middle (best ≠ current); streak ending \"yesterday\" still counts as current since \"today is not over yet\"; duplicate completions on the same day only count once (Set dedup).\n- `weekStart`: Monday-start logic across the Sunday→Monday boundary (JS `getDay()` returns 0 for Sunday — this is the classic off-by-one source).\n- `completionsInWeek`: boundary exactly at week start/end timestamps.\n- `computeBadges`: each of the 8 badges' `progress()` function at exactly its target, one below target, zero state; `'air-explorer'` badge when `quiz.total` is `null` (never taken) vs a taken quiz; `'weekly'` badge depends on `s.weeklyGoal`, which is itself mutable via `SET_WEEKLY_GOAL`.\n- `computeMilestones`: `count` exactly matching a milestone value (is it in `reached` or still `next`?); count beyond the last milestone (20) → `next: null`.\n- `planStats`: empty plan → `ratio: 0` (not `NaN` from 0/0).\n\n**Test skeleton:**\n```js\nimport { test, describe } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport {\n  INITIAL_STATE, sanitizeState, reducer, computePoints, computeStreak,\n  weekStart, completionsInWeek, computeBadges, computeMilestones, planStats, isInPlan,\n} from '../../features/progress/progress.js';\n\ndescribe('sanitizeState robustness', () => {\n  for (const bad of [null, undefined, 'garbage', [], 42, { plan: 'not-an-array' }]) {\n    test(`never throws on ${JSON.stringify(bad)}`, () => {\n      assert.doesNotThrow(() => sanitizeState(bad));\n    });\n  }\n  test('drops plan items missing id/refId', () => {\n    const s = sanitizeState({ plan: [{ title: 'no id' }] });\n    assert.equal(s.plan.length, 0);\n  });\n  test('clamps out-of-range difficulty to [1,3]', () => {\n    const s = sanitizeState({ plan: [{ id: 'a', refId: 'r', difficulty: 99 }] });\n    assert.equal(s.plan[0].difficulty, 3);\n  });\n  test('rejects malformed deadline strings', () => {\n    const s = sanitizeState({ plan: [{ id: 'a', refId: 'r', deadline: 'next tuesday' }] });\n    assert.equal(s.plan[0].deadline, null);\n  });\n  test('checklist indices outside [0,50) are filtered', () => {\n    const s = sanitizeState({ checklists: { intro: [1, 5, 99, -1] } });\n    assert.deepEqual(s.checklists.intro, [1, 5]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('reducer: ADD_PLAN_ITEM dedup', () => {\n  test('adding an already-planned (kind,refId) is a no-op (same reference)', () => {\n    const s1 = reducer(INITIAL_STATE, { type: 'ADD_PLAN_ITEM', item: { kind: 'action', refId: 'x' }, id: '1', now: 'now' });\n    const s2 = reducer(s1, { type: 'ADD_PLAN_ITEM', item: { kind: 'action', refId: 'x' }, id: '2', now: 'now' });\n    assert.equal(s2, s1); // referential equality matters: store.js uses it to skip persisting\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('reducer: TOGGLE_COMPLETE / REMOVE_PLAN_ITEM', () => {\n  test('REMOVE_PLAN_ITEM keeps history (does not erase past completion)', () => {\n    let s = reducer(INITIAL_STATE, { type: 'ADD_PLAN_ITEM', item: { kind: 'action', refId: 'x', difficulty: 1 }, id: 'p1', now: 'now' });\n    s = reducer(s, { type: 'TOGGLE_COMPLETE', id: 'p1', historyId: 'h1', now: 'now' });\n    s = reducer(s, { type: 'REMOVE_PLAN_ITEM', id: 'p1' });\n    assert.equal(s.plan.length, 0);\n    assert.equal(s.history.length, 1);\n  });\n  test('toggling complete off removes matching history entry only', () => {\n    let s = reducer(INITIAL_STATE, { type: 'ADD_PLAN_ITEM', item: { kind: 'action', refId: 'x', difficulty: 1 }, id: 'p1', now: 'now' });\n    s = reducer(s, { type: 'TOGGLE_COMPLETE', id: 'p1', historyId: 'h1', now: 'now' });\n    s = reducer(s, { type: 'TOGGLE_COMPLETE', id: 'p1', historyId: 'ignored', now: 'later' });\n    assert.equal(s.history.length, 0);\n    assert.equal(s.plan[0].completedAt, null);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('reducer: RECORD_QUIZ bestScore', () => {\n  test('first attempt sets bestScore even if 0', () => {\n    const s = reducer(INITIAL_STATE, { type: 'RECORD_QUIZ', score: 0, total: 10, now: 'now' });\n    assert.equal(s.quiz.bestScore, 0);\n  });\n  test('worse re-attempt does not lower bestScore', () => {\n    let s = reducer(INITIAL_STATE, { type: 'RECORD_QUIZ', score: 8, total: 10, now: 'now' });\n    s = reducer(s, { type: 'RECORD_QUIZ', score: 3, total: 10, now: 'later' });\n    assert.equal(s.quiz.bestScore, 8);\n    assert.equal(s.quiz.lastScore, 3);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('reducer: RESET_PROGRESS preserves proposals', () => {\n  test('clears plan/history/quiz but keeps proposals', () => {\n    let s = reducer(INITIAL_STATE, { type: 'ADD_PROPOSAL', proposal: { title: 'Idea' }, id: 'idea1', now: 'now' });\n    s = reducer(s, { type: 'ADD_PLAN_ITEM', item: { kind: 'action', refId: 'x' }, id: 'p1', now: 'now' });\n    s = reducer(s, { type: 'RESET_PROGRESS' });\n    assert.equal(s.plan.length, 0);\n    assert.equal(s.proposals.length, 1);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('reducer: unknown action', () => {\n  test('returns same state reference', () => {\n    assert.equal(reducer(INITIAL_STATE, { type: 'NOPE' }), INITIAL_STATE);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('computeStreak', () => {\n  test('empty history -> {current:0, best:0}', () => {\n    assert.deepEqual(computeStreak([]), { current: 0, best: 0 });\n  });\n  test('duplicate completions same day count once', () => {\n    const now = new Date(2026, 9, 14);\n    const h = [{ completedAt: new Date(2026,9,14,9).toISOString() }, { completedAt: new Date(2026,9,14,18).toISOString() }];\n    assert.deepEqual(computeStreak(h, now), { current: 1, best: 1 });\n  });\n  test('gap in the middle: best > current', () => {\n    const now = new Date(2026, 9, 14);\n    const h = [\n      { completedAt: new Date(2026,9,1).toISOString() },\n      { completedAt: new Date(2026,9,2).toISOString() },\n      { completedAt: new Date(2026,9,3).toISOString() },\n      // gap\n      { completedAt: new Date(2026,9,14).toISOString() },\n    ];\n    const r = computeStreak(h, now);\n    assert.equal(r.best, 3);\n    assert.equal(r.current, 1);\n  });\n  test('streak ending yesterday still counts as current (\"today not over\")', () => {\n    const now = new Date(2026, 9, 14, 8); // morning, haven't logged today yet\n    const h = [{ completedAt: new Date(2026,9,13).toISOString() }];\n    assert.equal(computeStreak(h, now).current, 1);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('weekStart', () => {\n  test('Sunday maps back to previous Monday (not forward)', () => {\n    const sunday = new Date(2026, 9, 18); // a Sunday\n    const start = weekStart(sunday);\n    assert.equal(start.getDay(), 1);\n    assert.equal(start.getDate(), 12);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('computeMilestones', () => {\n  test('count exactly at a milestone is included in reached', () => {\n    const history = Array.from({ length: 5 }, () => ({}));\n    const m = computeMilestones(history);\n    assert.ok(m.reached.includes(5));\n    assert.equal(m.next, 10);\n  });\n  test('beyond last milestone -> next is null', () => {\n    const history = Array.from({ length: 25 }, () => ({}));\n    assert.equal(computeMilestones(history).next, null);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('planStats', () => {\n  test('empty plan -> ratio 0, not NaN', () => {\n    assert.deepEqual(planStats([]), { total: 0, done: 0, open: 0, ratio: 0 });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('computePoints', () => {\n  test('null bestScore contributes 0, not NaN', () => {\n    const s = { ...INITIAL_STATE, history: [], quiz: { ...INITIAL_STATE.quiz, bestScore: null }, proposals: [] };\n    assert.equal(computePoints(s).fromQuiz, 0);\n  });\n  test('proposals capped at MAX_COUNTED_PROPOSALS even if more exist', () => {\n    const s = { ...INITIAL_STATE, proposals: Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, i) => ({ id: String(i) })) };\n    assert.equal(computePoints(s).fromProposals, 3 * 15);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. `features/progress/store.js` — integration gaps\n\nThis wraps `progress.js` with `localStorage` persistence and cross-tab sync (`useSyncExternalStore`). None of this is tested, and it's exactly the kind of wiring where unit-tested pieces (`reducer`, `readJSON`) can still integrate incorrectly.\n\n**Integration gaps:**\n- `havoActions.addToPlan()` → `writeJSON` is actually called with the new state, and `isPersistenceAvailable()` reflects write failures (simulate `localStorage.setItem` throwing).\n- Cross-tab sync: a `storage` event for `STORAGE_KEY` updates in-memory `state` and notifies listeners; an event for a *different* key is ignored.\n- `getServerSnapshot()` always returns `INITIAL_STATE` (SSR/hydration safety) regardless of what's in `localStorage` — this is the no-hydration-mismatch guarantee and deserves an explicit regression test.\n- First `subscribe()` call lazily loads from storage exactly once (`ensureLoaded` idempotency) and attaches the window `storage` listener only when the first listener subscribes, removing it when the last unsubscribes.\n- `dispatch` short-circuits (does not call `writeJSON`/`emit`) when the reducer returns the same state reference (ties back to the `ADD_PLAN_ITEM` dedup case above) — worth a spy-based test asserting `writeJSON` call count.\n\n**Test skeleton** (needs a minimal fake `window`/`localStorage`/event target — this module is a good candidate for adding `jsdom`, or hand-roll a tiny fake since the surface used is small):\n```js\nimport { test, describe, beforeEach } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n\nfunction installFakeWindow() {\n  const store = new Map();\n  const listeners = new Map(); // type -> Set<fn>\n  global.window = {\n    localStorage: {\n      getItem: (k) => (store.has(k) ? store.get(k) : null),\n      setItem: (k, v) => store.set(k, v),\n    },\n    addEventListener: (type, fn) => { (listeners.get(type) ?? listeners.set(type, new Set()).get(type)).add(fn); },\n    removeEventListener: (type, fn) => listeners.get(type)?.delete(fn),\n  };\n  return { store, fire: (type, evt) => listeners.get(type)?.forEach((fn) => fn(evt)) };\n}\n\ndescribe('progress store integration', () => {\n  let fakeWin;\n  beforeEach(async (t) => {\n    fakeWin = installFakeWindow();\n    t.after(() => { delete global.window; });\n    // store.js caches module-level state; re-import with cache-busting query per test\n  });\n\n  test('getServerSnapshot always returns INITIAL_STATE regardless of localStorage contents', async () => {\n    fakeWin.store.set('havo:v1', JSON.stringify({ plan: [{ id: '1', refId: 'r' }] }));\n    const { useHavoState } = await import(`../../features/progress/store.js?t=${Date.now()}`);\n    // exercised via renderHook in a React-aware test environment; assert the\n    // server snapshot function itself is pure INITIAL_STATE if exported/testable.\n  });\n\n  test('a storage event for a different key is ignored', async () => {\n    const mod = await import(`../../features/progress/store.js?t=${Date.now()}1`);\n    fakeWin.fire('storage', { key: 'some-other-app:v1' });\n    // assert internal state unchanged (requires exposing a snapshot getter, or\n    // testing indirectly through havoActions + a subscribed listener spy).\n  });\n\n  test('dispatch does not call localStorage.setItem when reducer is a no-op', async () => {\n    const { havoActions } = await import(`../../features/progress/store.js?t=${Date.now()}2`);\n    let calls = 0;\n    const realSetItem = fakeWin.store.set.bind(fakeWin.store);\n    global.window.localStorage.setItem = (...args) => { calls++; return realSetItem(...args); };\n    havoActions.addToPlan({ kind: 'action', refId: 'dup' });\n    const before = calls;\n    havoActions.addToPlan({ kind: 'action', refId: 'dup' }); // duplicate, should no-op\n    assert.equal(calls, before);\n  });\n});\n```\n*(Note: because `store.js` holds module-level mutable state, tests must either re-import with a cache-busting query string per test, as sketched, or the module should be refactored to expose a reset/factory function for testability — flagging this as a design gap too.)*\n\n---\n\n## 8. `features/actions/finder.js`\n\n**Untested function:** `recommendActions` (the whole ranking/filtering engine).\n\n**Edge cases not covered:**\n- Hard filters: `timeBucket` greater than requested time excluded; `cost` rank exceeding `budget` rank excluded (verify `COST_RANK` ordering `free(0) < low(1) < flexible(2)`).\n- An action matching **neither** `setting` nor `activity` is excluded entirely (the \"soft constraints, but at least one must match\" rule) — easy to get wrong in either direction.\n- Scoring: setting match +3, activity match +3, mode match +2, plus the short-session/easy-difficulty +1 nudge when `time <= 2 && difficulty === 1`.\n- Sort order: primary by score desc, tie-broken by `difficulty` asc — needs a fixture with a tie.\n- `MAX_RESULTS` (6) cap — more than 6 matches must be truncated.\n- Missing/partial `answers` merge with `DEFAULT_FINDER_ANSWERS` (e.g. calling with `{}`).\n- Empty `actions` array → `[]`, not throw.\n- `reasons`/`cautions` content correctness for the group-mode-without-group-action case vs solo-without-group.\n\n**Test skeleton:**\n```js\nimport { test, describe } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { recommendActions, MAX_RESULTS, DEFAULT_FINDER_ANSWERS } from '../../features/actions/finder.js';\n\nconst mkAction = (over) => ({\n  id: 'a', title: 'A', timeBucket: 1, cost: 'free', settings: ['school'],\n  activities: ['learning'], mode: 'solo', difficulty: 1, ...over,\n});\n\ndescribe('recommendActions hard filters', () => {\n  test('excludes actions needing more time than available', () => {\n    const r = recommendActions({ time: 1 }, [mkAction({ timeBucket: 3 })]);\n    assert.equal(r.length, 0);\n  });\n  test('excludes actions costlier than budget allows', () => {\n    const r = recommendActions({ budget: 'free' }, [mkAction({ cost: 'flexible' })]);\n    assert.equal(r.length, 0);\n  });\n  test('excludes action matching neither setting nor activity', () => {\n    const r = recommendActions(\n      { setting: 'home', activity: 'creating' },\n      [mkAction({ settings: ['school'], activities: ['learning'] })],\n    );\n    assert.equal(r.length, 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('recommendActions scoring & ranking', () => {\n  test('ties on score are broken by lower difficulty first', () => {\n    const easy = mkAction({ id: 'easy', difficulty: 1 });\n    const hard = mkAction({ id: 'hard', difficulty: 3 });\n    const r = recommendActions({ time: 3 }, [hard, easy]); // time>2 avoids the difficulty-1 nudge\n    assert.equal(r[0].action.id, 'easy');\n  });\n  test('caps results at MAX_RESULTS', () => {\n    const many = Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, i) => mkAction({ id: `a${i}` }));\n    assert.equal(recommendActions({}, many).length, MAX_RESULTS);\n  });\n  test('missing answers fall back to DEFAULT_FINDER_ANSWERS', () => {\n    assert.doesNotThrow(() => recommendActions({}, [mkAction({})]));\n  });\n  test('empty actions list -> empty results, no throw', () => {\n    assert.deepEqual(recommendActions({}, []), []);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. `features/initiatives/proposal.js`\n\n**Untested functions:** `containsContact`, `validateProposal`, `toStoredProposal`.\n\n**Edge cases not covered:**\n- `containsContact`: true positives (`+998 90 123 45 67`, `name@example.com`), and crucially **false positives/negatives** since this gates a minors-focused form — e.g. does a `description` with \"позвони мне 90123456\" get caught? Does a sentence containing a long number that *isn't* a phone (like \"в 2024 году собрали 15000000 сум\") get wrongly flagged? This needs explicit test coverage given the regex is heuristic.\n- `validateProposal`: boundary lengths at exactly `min`/`max` for `title` and `description` (off-by-one on `<`/`>`); `category` not present in the provided `categories` map; `place`/`participants` not in the allowed option lists; `consent` false; contact info detected independently in `title`, `description`, and `alias` (three separate branches).\n- `toStoredProposal`: trims whitespace from `title`/`description`/`alias`; coerces `needsAdult` to boolean.\n\n**Test skeleton:**\n```js\nimport { test, describe } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { containsContact, validateProposal, toStoredProposal, LIMITS, EMPTY_PROPOSAL } from '../../features/initiatives/proposal.js';\n\ndescribe('containsContact', () => {\n  test('detects phone numbers', () => assert.ok(containsContact('звони +998 90 123 45 67')));\n  test('detects emails', () => assert.ok(containsContact('пиши на test@example.com')));\n  test('plain text without contact info is clean', () => assert.ok(!containsContact('Соберём мусор во дворе школы')));\n  test('large non-phone numbers do not false-positive (documents current regex behavior)', () => {\n    // This locks down current behavior; if it turns out to false-positive, that's a bug to fix, not hide.\n    containsContact('В 2024 году collected 15000000 сум');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('validateProposal boundaries', () => {\n  const categories = { school: {} };\n  const valid = { title: 'A'.repeat(10), category: 'school', place: 'school', description: 'B'.repeat(40), participants: '1-3', consent: true, alias: '' };\n\n  test('title exactly at min length passes', () => {\n    assert.equal(validateProposal({ ...valid, title: 'A'.repeat(LIMITS.title.min) }, categories).title, undefined);\n  });\n  test('title one below min length fails', () => {\n    assert.ok(validateProposal({ ...valid, title: 'A'.repeat(LIMITS.title.min - 1) }, categories).title);\n  });\n  test('category not in provided categories map fails', () => {\n    assert.ok(validateProposal({ ...valid, category: 'unknown' }, categories).category);\n  });\n  test('consent=false always fails regardless of other fields', () => {\n    assert.ok(validateProposal({ ...valid, consent: false }, categories).consent);\n  });\n  test('contact info in alias is caught independently of title/description', () => {\n    assert.equal(validateProposal({ ...valid, alias: 'call me@x.com' }, categories).alias, expect_message());\n    function expect_message() { return validateProposal({ ...valid, alias: 'x@y.com' }, categories).alias; }\n  });\n  test('fully valid payload returns empty errors object', () => {\n    assert.deepEqual(validateProposal(valid, categories), {});\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('toStoredProposal', () => {\n  test('trims whitespace and coerces needsAdult to boolean', () => {\n    const stored = toStoredProposal({ ...EMPTY_PROPOSAL, title: '  Hi  ', description: '  desc  ', needsAdult: 1 });\n    assert.equal(stored.title, 'Hi');\n    assert.equal(stored.needsAdult, true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. `features/problem/inversionSim.js`\n\nDeterministic (seeded PRNG) despite simulating a particle system — genuinely unit-testable and currently has zero coverage.\n\n**Untested functions:** `buildLayout`, `createSim`, `step`, `settle`, `levelBand`, `explain`.\n\n**Edge cases not covered:**\n- `buildLayout(w,h)` is deterministic for given `w,h` (same seed 42) — snapshot the buildings/chimneys count and bounds.\n- `step`: inversion lid behavior (`p.y` clamped to `lidY` and bounced) only triggers when `inversion` is true; ground collision clamps `p.y` to `groundY-2`; `rain` randomly removes particles (probabilistic — test over many iterations that rain reduces particle count on average, or inject a seeded sim and check determinism).\n- `MAX_PARTICLES` cap (900): after many `step()` calls with full traffic/heating, `sim.particles.length` never exceeds 900.\n- `settle()` runs `frames` steps with `animateCars:false` and sets `sim.level` directly from `zoneLevel` (no smoothing) — distinct behavior from `step()`'s exponential smoothing, worth a dedicated test.\n- `levelBand`: boundaries at exactly 30 and 60.\n- `explain()`: all 6 branches (no sources; inversion+calm; inversion+wind; rain; strong wind; default) — each is a distinct `if` with no fallthrough test currently.\n\n**Test skeleton:**\n```js\nimport { test, describe } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { buildLayout, createSim, step, settle, levelBand, explain, WIND_SPEEDS } from '../../features/problem/inversionSim.js';\n\ndescribe('buildLayout', () => {\n  test('is deterministic for the same dimensions (fixed seed)', () => {\n    const a = buildLayout(800, 400);\n    const b = buildLayout(800, 400);\n    assert.deepEqual(a.buildings, b.buildings);\n    assert.deepEqual(a.chimneys, b.chimneys);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('step', () => {\n  test('respects MAX_PARTICLES cap over many frames', () => {\n    const layout = buildLayout(800, 400);\n    const sim = createSim(layout);\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3000; i++) step(sim, { inversion: true, wind: 0, rain: false, traffic: 3, heating: 3 });\n    assert.ok(sim.particles.length <= 900);\n  });\n  test('inversion keeps particles below the lid (lidY)', () => {\n    const layout = buildLayout(800, 400);\n    const sim = createSim(layout);\n    for (let i = 0; i < 500; i++) step(sim, { inversion: true, wind: 0, rain: false, traffic: 3, heating: 3 });\n    for (const p of sim.particles) assert.ok(p.y >= layout.lidY - 5);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('settle', () => {\n  test('sets level directly from instantaneous zoneLevel (no smoothing lag)', () => {\n    const layout = buildLayout(800, 400);\n    const sim = createSim(layout);\n    settle(sim, { inversion: true, wind: 0, rain: false, traffic: 3, heating: 3 }, 1600);\n    assert.ok(sim.level >= 0 && sim.level <= 100);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('levelBand', () => {\n  test('boundary at 30', () => { assert.equal(levelBand(29.9).id, 'low'); assert.equal(levelBand(30).id, 'mid'); });\n  test('boundary at 60', () => { assert.equal(levelBand(59.9).id, 'mid'); assert.equal(levelBand(60).id, 'high'); });\n});\n\ndescribe('explain', () => {\n  test('no sources', () => assert.match(explain({ traffic: 0, heating: 0, inversion: false, wind: 0, rain: false }), /Источников нет/));\n  test('inversion + calm', () => assert.match(explain({ traffic: 1, heating: 0, inversion: true, wind: 0, rain: false }), /Инверсия и безветрие/));\n  test('inversion + wind', () => assert.match(explain({ traffic: 1, heating: 0, inversion: true, wind: 1, rain: false }), /частично выносит/));\n  test('rain', () => assert.match(explain({ traffic: 1, heating: 0, inversion: false, wind: 0, rain: true }), /Осадки вымывают/));\n  test('strong wind', () => assert.match(explain({ traffic: 1, heating: 0, inversion: false, wind: 2, rain: false }), /Сильный ветер/));\n  test('default calm-clear case', () => assert.match(explain({ traffic: 1, heating: 0, inversion: false, wind: 1, rain: false }), /становится холоднее/));\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. Small modules worth quick coverage\n\n**`features/planner/planItems.js`** — `actionToPlanItem`, `initiativeToPlanItem`:\n```js\nimport { test } from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { actionToPlanItem, initiativeToPlanItem } from '../../features/planner/planItems.js';\n\ntest('actionToPlanItem maps fields 1:1 with kind \"action\"', () => {\n  const pi = actionToPlanItem({ id: 'a1', title: 'T', category: 'c', effect: 'direct', mode: 'solo', difficulty: 2 });\n  assert.equal(pi.kind, 'action');\n  assert.equal(pi.refId, 'a1');\n});\n\ntest('initiativeToPlanItem maps unknown category to community effect fallback', () => {\n  const pi = initiativeToPlanItem({ id: 'i1', name: 'N', category: 'unknown-cat', difficulty: 1 });\n  assert.equal(pi.effect, 'community');\n  assert.equal(pi.mode, 'group'); // always group, regardless of input\n});\n```\n\n**`data/cities.js`** — `getCityById`:\n```js\ntest('getCityById returns null for unknown id', () => assert.equal(getCityById('atlantis'), null));\ntest('getCityById returns null for undefined/empty id', () => assert.equal(getCityById(undefined), null));\n```\n\n**`features/actions/actionSheetStore.js`, `features/tools/toolTabStore.js`** — module-level pub/sub, same caveat as `progress/store.js` (shared mutable state across tests). Worth at minimum:\n```js\ntest('openAction/closeAction notify subscribed listeners', () => {\n  let notified = 0;\n  const unsub = subscribe(() => notified++);\n  openAction('x');\n  closeAction();\n  unsub();\n  assert.equal(notified, 2);\n});\n```\n(`subscribe` isn't exported from `actionSheetStore.js` currently — would need to export it, or test only through `useOpenActionId` with a React-aware harness.)\n\n---\n\n## Missing integration tests (cross-module, currently zero)\n\n1. **Plan → complete → points/badges pipeline**: `actionToPlanItem()` → `havoActions.addToPlan()` → `havoActions.toggleComplete()` → `computePoints`/`computeBadges` reflect the change end-to-end. Each piece is unit-testable alone, but nothing currently verifies they compose correctly.\n2. **Quiz → store**: `Quiz.js` calls `havoActions.recordQuiz(score, total)` on finishing — no test verifies the UI's `score` calculation (`answers.filter(a => a.chosen === a.correct).length`) matches what's persisted, nor that `resultMessage()`'s ratio thresholds (0.9/0.7/0.4) align with `QUIZ_PASS_RATIO`.\n3. **API route → `normalizeWaqi` → `AirDashboard` rendering**: the route and the normalizer are each testable in isolation, but nothing exercises the full fetch→normalize→render chain for each `status` (`ok`, `unconfigured`, `no-station`, `no-data`, `error`) to confirm `StatusPanel` picks the right branch — a response-shape change in one place could silently stop matching the switch in the other.\n4. **LocalStorage corruption → store → UI**: if `localStorage` contains data from an older schema (`version` mismatch) or is tampered with, `sanitizeState` should degrade gracefully — no test currently feeds genuinely adversarial/corrupted blobs through the *whole* `store.js` → `progress.js` path (only through `sanitizeState` directly, which itself has no tests either).\n5. **Cross-tab sync**: two \"tabs\" (two subscribed listeners) seeing a `storage` event and converging to the same state — currently architecturally supported but entirely unverified.\n6. **`ImpactCalculator` UI ↔ `impact.js` math**: the component recomputes `carFactor` based on `factorMode` ('epa' vs 'custom') before calling `calculateImpact` — no test confirms switching the toggle actually swaps which factor feeds the calculation (this requires React Testing Library, which isn't installed).\n",
